<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo noupdate="1">

    <!--
        Selling price tiers.

        A reseller's whole business is the gap between the buy price and the sell
        price, and that gap is different for a wholesaler taking a pallet than
        for a shop taking a carton. Odoo models that with pricelists, one per
        tier, assigned on the customer record so the correct price follows the
        CUSTOMER rather than depending on a salesperson remembering.

        These are deliberately EMPTY SHELLS - no price rules. The rules are
        commercial decisions, not configuration, and they change far more often
        than this module does. Add them in Sales > Products > Pricelists once the
        real buy prices are known: typically a percentage off the sale price, or
        a formula on cost with a minimum margin.

        DO NOT set a rule based on cost until the first receipt AND its landed
        costs are posted. Cost is 0.00 on a freshly imported product, so a
        margin-on-cost rule would price everything at zero and the sales team
        would find out before you did.

        THE "PRICELISTS" SETTING MUST BE ON, AND IT IS NOT OPTIONAL HERE.
        Sales > Settings > Pricing > Pricelists. Leaving it off does not merely
        hide the menu and leave these records dormant - res_config_settings
        .set_values() in the `product` module runs

            elif not self.group_product_pricelist:
                self.env['product.pricelist'].sudo().search([]).action_archive()

        on EVERY save of the Settings page. The domain is search([]), so saving
        Settings even once while the box is unchecked archives all three of
        these, whether or not anyone touched the pricelist toggle. Odoo warns
        with "You are deactivating the pricelist feature. Every active pricelist
        will be archived." - that warning is literal, and it fires because these
        records exist.

        Currency is left unset so each pricelist takes the company currency; set
        it explicitly only on a pricelist that genuinely quotes in another
        currency.
    -->

    <record id="pricelist_wholesale" model="product.pricelist">
        <field name="name">Wholesale</field>
        <field name="sequence">10</field>
    </record>

    <record id="pricelist_retail" model="product.pricelist">
        <field name="name">Retail</field>
        <field name="sequence">20</field>
    </record>

    <!-- Export customers. Pair this with the Export - Zero Rated fiscal position
         on the customer record: the pricelist sets the price, the fiscal position
         sets the tax. Neither does the other's job. -->
    <record id="pricelist_export" model="product.pricelist">
        <field name="name">Export</field>
        <field name="sequence">30</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
